findings.body:
The assertion uses `&&` where the message says "match one of". The old pattern matches the "Refused to frame ... because an ancestor violates" message, and the new one matches "Framing ... violates". A single browser log line cannot match both, so `IsMatch(old) && IsMatch(new)` is always false and the test always fails.

The intent is an either-or check across browser versions. Use `||`.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}

::suggestion{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="107-110"}
Assert.True(
    ParseErrorMessageRegexOld.IsMatch(logs[0].Message) ||
    ParseErrorMessageRegexNew.IsMatch(logs[0].Message),
    $"Expected log message to match one of the CSP error patterns: {ParseErrorMessageRegexOld} or {ParseErrorMessageRegexNew}. Actual: {logs[0].Message}");

The internal source-build step used to pass `dotnetbuilds.blob.core.windows.net/internal` and its read token. It now passes `https://ci.dot.net/internal` with the same `$(dotnetbuilds-internal-container-read-token-base64)` as both the feed URL and the feed key. This is a runtime-feed behavior change that goes beyond a version bump.

I could not confirm from the repo that `ci.dot.net/internal` serves the same content or accepts this token. If it doesn't, the internal source build will fail to restore the runtime. If it does, the token is now sent to a different host, so the host and its access scope should be confirmed.

